record legeos.evidence.file-sorting-and-view-modes-20260831/1 : evidence {
    title "Sorting and view modes: shared contract, both surfaces, bounded thumbnails, preferences — all checks green"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:dddc9187c434e9f122503403ff7af8c207624e50
    command "cargo test -p lege-filed -p lege-files sort; cargo test -p lege-shell -p lege-files view_mode; cargo test -p lege-shell -p lege-files thumbnail; cargo test -p lege-field -p lege-shell no_loose_file_tiles; cargo test -p lege-session-core file_view_preferences; just check"
    summary """
        One sort contract in lege_types::file_sort — natural name, kind, size, modified and manual-reference orders, deterministic and total with stable ascending tie breakers, direction flipping only the primary key, folder-first explicit — is what lege-filed serves and what Files and the shell's Home folder surfaces re-sort with; both surfaces switch between detail list and thumbnail grid preserving selection, focus and scroll, thumbnails load as capped visible-plus-lookahead batches through Files.Previews1 decoded off the render thread with stale generations dropped, tray contents never become tiles, and file-view preferences (global default plus independently-resetting per-path overrides) round-trip in lege-session-core behind the registered files.view-preferences key; full just check green.
        """
}

