        All seven command-method checks of the Home Field umbrella pass on the current tree: the text field matches the graphical one, keyboard completeness, layout stability with exact inverses (38 lege-field tests plus property suite), maximize semantics, no pixelkit API change needed (full just check green this session at 2ce3f03 and prior commits), shelving unmaps and unshelving restores in both lege-window and lege-comp, and the windows-cannot-be-lost trio holds. The two manual checks (bare-Super/fallback reveal parity at a real keyboard, and shell death ending a live reveal) remain for a hands-on desktop run — they need physical input and a live compositor.
        """
}

